course: dictionary
lesson: 4647
title: Historical: the past in words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Historical means to do with history, which is the past. When a history lesson asks about «historical objects», such as old coins and letters, it means things that come from long ago. Look for clues in the words around it.
explain: Historical also tells you whether a person or event really existed. A giant in a fairy tale is not historical, but a queen who really ruled long ago is a historical figure. A story set in the past that mixes real events with made-up people is «historical fiction».
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Many families spoke Russian at home for historical reasons.» If you swap in "for reasons from the past", it still makes sense, so historical means to do with the past here.
fact: Historical means to do with history, or the past.
fact: A historical figure is a person who really lived, not only a character in a legend or a fairy tale.
fact: A historical novel or film is set in the past, and it often mixes real events with made-up characters.
fact: Historical sources are things like old letters, pictures and objects that help us learn what happened long ago.
fact: «For historical reasons» means for reasons that come from things that happened in the past.
exercise: «The museum had many historical objects, like old coins.» What does historical mean? | Very large | Made up for a story | *To do with the past | Brand new
exercise: Which one is a historical figure? | A talking fox from a fairy tale | A wizard in a film | *A queen who really ruled long ago | A dragon in a legend
exercise: «Mia read a historical novel about the Romans.» What kind of book is it? | A cookery book | A book about the weather | A book of maps | *A story set in the past
test: «Many families spoke Russian at home for historical reasons.» What does historical reasons mean here? | Reasons about the weather | *Reasons from the past | Reasons from a film | Reasons that nobody knows
test: Which one is a historical source? | A made-up comic about aliens | A cartoon of a dragon | *An old letter written a hundred years ago | A pop song
exam: Which word tells you a person really lived, not only in a legend? | *Historical | Imaginary | Fictional | Magical
